WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.342
Now we combine the two structures in one order-processing example.

00:00:04.342 --> 00:00:09.557
The dictionary totals_by_channel keeps a running sales total for each channel.

00:00:09.557 --> 00:00:14.100
The set unique_customers stores customer IDs without duplicates.

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:20.352
C101 appears twice, but the set still counts that customer only once.

00:00:20.352 --> 00:00:25.342
The dictionary, however, adds both web orders to the web total.

00:00:25.342 --> 00:00:32.322
This is a nice example of choosing a structure based on the question: dictionaries for labeled totals,

00:00:32.322 --> 00:00:34.131
sets for uniqueness.
